From 3d15cf240de30f5a90aed8674b619d7646944b07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thom Hadfield <100659456+festeraeb@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 07:22:28 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] libr3d: build on gfx103x (RDNA2): WMMA results via
 ds_bpermute + dot2/dot4

Why: RDNA2 (gfx103x) has no wave-matrix unit; the four WMMA wrappers in r3d_common.h and the
two in r3dh_wmma.h were the only reason 18 libr3d files did not build for gfx1031 (RX 6700 XT).
The new header gives the same 16x16x16 results with ds_bpermute and v_dot2/v_dot4, same
fragment layout; it is empty on every other target, so gfx11 builds are unchanged. The load
gate and CMake pattern admit gfx103x.
Revert: drop r3d_wmma_rdna2.h and its includes, restore the ^gfx11 pattern and the 11xxxx check.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
